 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Bounds Checking**: The accessor methods (`getCell`, neighbor calculations) assume the caller performs bounds checking. No internal clamping or boundary validation is implemented [S1, unofficial]. Accessing out-of-bounds indices will result in undefined behavior or memory errors.
-*   **Vertex Offset Interpretation**: The vertex position calculation relies on `vertexOffset` being stored in voxel units relative to the cell's grid position. If the offset is intended to be in world units, the multiplication by `voxel_size` must be adjusted [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Bounds Checking**: The accessor methods assume the caller performs bounds checking before accessing cells or vertices [S1, unofficial]. No internal clamping or boundary validation is implemented [S1, unofficial]. Accessing out-of-bounds indices will result in undefined behavior or memory errors [S1, unofficial].
 
